---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import Sheet from '../layouts/Sheet.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/url';
import '../styles/home.css';   // the same rows and the same card treatment as the index
import '../styles/about.css';
import portrait from '../assets/img/about-portrait.png';
import sketch1 from '../assets/img/about-sketch-1.png';
import sketch2 from '../assets/img/about-sketch-2.png';
import studio1 from '../assets/img/about-studio-1.png';
import studio2 from '../assets/img/about-studio-2.png';
import home1 from '../assets/img/about-home-1.png';
import home2 from '../assets/img/about-home-2.png';
import michigan from '../assets/img/about-michigan.jpg';

// The same eight pictures the Webflow About page used, framed like the project cards on the index:
// 24px radius, no hairline, the image covering the frame, every frame 3:2. The portrait is the
// hero's figure, cropped half-length with the figure on the left third. Each chapter is the index's
// row — the years at column 1, the words on the reading column from 6 — and carries its pictures
// beneath the words as the cards do: a pair of halves after each paragraph that has one, or a
// single under the words. No hairline in the body: sections are parted by air.
const hero = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [720, 1100, 1600, 2036], sizes: '(max-width: 767px) 164vw, (max-width: 1440px) 151vw, 2041px', loading: 'eager' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };
const half = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [480, 720, 1100, 1440], sizes: '(max-width: 767px) 100vw, (max-width: 1440px) 45vw, 612px', loading: 'lazy' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };
const single = { formats: ['avif', 'webp'] as const, widths: [720, 1100, 1440], sizes: '(max-width: 1023px) 100vw, (max-width: 1440px) 53vw, 718px', loading: 'lazy' as const, decoding: 'async' as const };

// The work the story names, where the index already links it.
const curio = 'https://www.figma.com/design/BiXcn2d7kNwzXtuw1aUGDx/Curio-Work?node-id=0-1';
const droploft = 'https://www.figma.com/design/3nUKfaJoAkZQdlZwzpyFff/Dify-Demos?node-id=0-1';
const observe = 'https://github.com/KyleXu0420/observe';

const facts = [
  { label: 'Worked with', items: ['Temper', 'Dify (LangGenius)', 'Curio Digital Therapeutics', 'Infloww', 'Heygen', 'Eaton Corporation', 'HIL Architects', 'ColdMe', 'COIL Connect for Virtual Exchange', 'Capital Area District Libraries', 'Erb Family Foundation'] },
  { label: 'Studied at', items: ['University of Michigan', "Xi'an University of Architecture and Technology"] },
  { label: 'Skills', items: ['AI UX', 'Agent workflows', 'Design systems', 'Design-to-code', 'Frontend prototyping', 'Design ops', 'Information architecture', 'Product strategy', 'UX research', 'Usability testing'] },
  { label: 'Tools', items: ['Figma', 'Claude Code', 'Cursor', 'Codex', 'React', 'TypeScript', 'Tailwind', 'HTML / CSS', 'JavaScript', 'Vitest', 'Python'] },
  { label: 'Languages', items: ['English', 'Mandarin (native)'] },
];
---
<Sheet
  title="About — Kyle Xu"
  description="Kyle Xu, AI product designer. Trained as an architect, then in HCI at the University of Michigan; since 2022 at Eaton, Heygen, Infloww, Curio Digital Therapeutics, Dify and Temper."
  ogImage="/og-about.jpg"
>
  <section class="col hero" aria-labelledby="h1">
    <h1 class="display claim" id="h1">At fifteen I was sketching buildings <span class="nb">instead of studying</span> <span class="nb">for the gaokao.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead deck">I trained as an architect. Now I decide what an AI agent is allowed to do.</p>
    <div class="photo portrait"><Picture src={portrait} {...hero} alt="Kyle in kendo uniform, holding a helmet, in front of a wall of labelled equipment shelves" /></div>
  </section>

  <section class="col sec" aria-label="Organisations, skills, tools and languages">
    <dl class="facts">
      {facts.map((f) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="meta">{f.label}</dt>
          <dd>{f.items.map((it, i) => <><span class="nb">{it}{i < f.items.length - 1 && ','}</span>{i < f.items.length - 1 && ' '}</>)}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="col sec" aria-label="How I got here">
    <ul class="tl story">
      <li>
        <span class="when">2013 – 2019</span>
        <div class="what">
          <p>Alongside the sketches I was in volunteer building workshops in Hangzhou, making small physical improvements. By 2017 I was being paid to design spaces and art pieces for my father's business associates. At eighteen a local design studio took me on for my first professional project. I got into architecture school in Xi'an.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <div class="photo"><Picture src={sketch1} {...half} alt="Kyle as a student, sitting on the steps of a rooftop garden" /></div>
          <div class="photo"><Picture src={sketch2} {...half} alt="Kyle's reflection in the window of a brick building, camera raised" /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="what">
          <p>In 2019, <span class="nb">part-time</span> at an <span class="nb">urban-design</span> practice, I learned that cost and construction decide more of a building than the drawing does. A junior architect's title counted for little outside architecture, so I found my own clients while still a student.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <div class="photo"><Picture src={studio1} {...half} alt="A small studio interior: a long wooden table and a glass partition" /></div>
          <div class="photo right"><Picture src={studio2} {...half} alt="A narrow city street lined with shop signs" /></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="when">2020 – 2022</span>
        <div class="what">
          <p>I spent those three years at home, on UI and UX projects with partners in several Chinese cities. One of them was a digital platform for a community in Xi'an's Muslim Quarter, run jointly by my university and the city. With a few people from a film community I built and launched an app.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <div class="photo up"><Picture src={home1} {...half} alt="Kyle at a workbench in a workshop" /></div>
          <div class="photo mid"><Picture src={home2} {...half} alt="A night-market kitchen in Xi'an's Muslim Quarter, cooks at the grills" /></div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="when">2022 – now</span>
        <div class="what">
          <p>From then on all of the work was on screens. I interned at Eaton on an <a class="ref" href={href('/projects/eaton')}>IoT configuration tool</a> for airport clients, began the master's in HCI at the University of Michigan, and at Heygen <span class="nb">re-architected</span> <a class="ref" href={href('/projects/heygen')}>the AI video editor</a> around the script.</p>
          <p>At Infloww the product was a chat assistant for a B2B CRM, and most of the design turned out to be the work around the model. With the prompt engineers I designed the payment and messaging tools for the cases where it is wrong.</p>
          <p>At Curio Digital Therapeutics I was the founding product designer on <a class="ref" href={curio} rel="noopener">MamaLift and MenoLift</a>, two <span class="nb">FDA-cleared</span> products. The design system, the information architecture and a feature called the Achievement Garden all went through clinical review.</p>
          <p>In 2026, for Dify, an AI application platform, I designed <a class="ref" href={droploft} rel="noopener">Droploft</a>, a team knowledge base, Syncless, a <span class="nb">multi-agent</span> workplace concept, and Skills Agent for Dify Enterprise. At Temper I worked on contract inside the production codebase, on the <span class="nb">design-token</span> architecture and <a class="ref" href={observe} rel="noopener">the lint that enforces it</a>, so a rule holds whether or not a designer is watching.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pics">
          <div class="photo"><Picture src={michigan} {...single} alt="Kyle with classmates at the University of Michigan" /></div>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="signoff">
    <p class="stance">Architecture taught me to decide the parts and their limits before drawing anything. That is most of the job on an agent product.</p>
    <p>I am most useful once the model works and before the interface is settled. <span class="nb">If that</span> is your product, <a class="ref" href="mailto:kylexu@umich.edu">write to me</a>.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Sheet>
